# Dastro 3.4 — manual patch: lint guardrails and worktree setup

The pre-commit hook now runs ESLint and stylelint on staged files, plus
`npm test` when the project has a `test` script. These steps wire the shared
dastro rules into the project and leave it with **zero lint errors**, so the
next commit passes. Warnings (accessibility hints) may stay.

## 1. ESLint: add the shared dastro rules

In `eslint.config.mjs`, import the shared config and spread it right after
`...eslintPluginAstro.configs.recommended` (before project overrides):

```js
import dastroEslint from 'dastro/config/eslint';

export default defineConfig(
  // …existing presets…
  ...eslintPluginAstro.configs.recommended,
  ...dastroEslint,
  // …project overrides…
);
```

It adds the jsx-a11y preset as warnings, and two errors: `target="_blank"`
without `rel`, and an empty `title=""`. It needs `eslint-plugin-astro` and
`eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y` (boilerplate defaults); install whichever is missing
with `npm i -D`.

## 2. stylelint: add the config and the lint script

Create `stylelint.config.mjs` next to `package.json`:

```js
export { default } from 'dastro/config/stylelint';
```

stylelint ships with dastro; no install needed. Extend the `lint` script in
`package.json` so it covers styles:

```json
"lint": "eslint \"src/**/*.{js,mjs,ts,jsx,tsx,astro}\" && stylelint \"src/**/*.{css,scss,astro}\""
```

The rules: colours and fonts come from the token files
(`src/sass/root/_colors.scss`, `src/sass/typography/_font-types.scss`) — no hex,
named or literal `rgb()`/`hsl()` colours (`rgba(var(--x), .5)` is fine), no
absolute `font-size` (px/rem/pt) or literal `font-family` elsewhere — and no
`transition: all`. The pre-commit hook lints the same `src/` files as
`npm run lint`. Token files, print
styles and the styleguide/debug components are exempt.

## 3. Fix every lint error

Run `npm run lint` and fix each error at its source:

- **Colour literal** → the matching token (`var(--…)` from `_colors.scss`). A
  colour with no token gets one in `_colors.scss`, named for its role.
- **Font literal** → the design's font type (`$font-types` / `text-*` class) or
  a font token.
- **`transition: all`** → list the transitioned properties.
- **`target="_blank"` without `rel`** → use the `Link` component, or add
  `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- **Empty `title=""`** → omit the attribute.

A `stylelint-disable-next-line <rule> -- <reason>` comment is the last resort,
for a value that is genuinely outside the token system. Done when
`npm run lint` reports 0 errors. Check the changed modules in the browser
against production.

## 4. Worktree setup

If `.worktreeinclude` does not exist, create it with one line:

```
.env
```

Fresh worktrees are then set up with `npm ci && npx dastro worktree-setup`
(links the listed files from the main checkout and installs the git hooks).
If the project is used in T3 Code, set that command as the project's setup
script.
